  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "The act release is pinned and sha256-verified before extraction, the image is pinned as tag@digest with no floating tag, and `--artifact-server-path` is passed with the workflow untouched, but it chose v0.2.88 and the 20261007 image under a self-invented 14-day cooldown instead of the newest entries at least 7 days old (v0.2.89, 20261028), and nothing was run end to end."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 5,
        "rationale": "The workflow's upload step, the lists, the pages and the build and link-check scripts are untouched and the new env file is a reasonable config, but it edited the README (which was meant to stay unchanged), added a .gitignore, and added unrequested extras such as forcing the container architecture, an OS/arch gate and argument passthrough."
      },
      {
        "name": "explanation",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "It clearly explains what the artifact flag fixes, states that act does not tell you how long CI takes, flags its version choice as a judgement call and is honest that nothing was run, but its reason for skipping v0.2.89 and 20261028 rests on a two-week rule rather than the 7-day one, and the claim that the loop shows whether a job would exceed its 10-minute timeout partly undercuts the timing caveat."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 6.0
  },
